# Everything the build does not need. Keeping the context small is not only
# about speed: a stray coverage file or a local build of the binary would land
# in the image layer above, and a profile measured on this machine would be
# compiled into the binary everybody pulls. scripts/check-docker-context.sh
# holds this to a dirty checkout, and to every file git tracks.
.git
.github
.claude
bin
dist
docs
tmp
# `go build ./cmd/tls-forge` from the root drops the binary there. The root
# alone: cmd/tls-forge is the source of it.
tls-forge

# Dependencies and environments, wherever a package or an example keeps them.
**/node_modules
node/vendor
**/.venv*
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
python/src/tlsforge/bin

# A profile measured from the browser on this machine: everything under
# profile/data is compiled into the binary.
profile/data/local

# What running the tool and its tests leaves behind: a report written beside
# the run is named after the moment it began.
coverage.out
coverage.html
report-*.html
report-*.json

# Editors and OS
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
